div.p:
If it was to be conducted properly and in an expert manner, the work before such
                    a committee would be very onerous indeed, for it would embrace: 
                        1.

The whole existing and past systems for the collection and application
                            of revenues, internal as well as external;
                        2.

The Liberian frontier force;
                        3.

Railways, roads, and telegraphs;
                        4.

Harbours, shipping, and coastal communications;
                        5.

Agriculture;
